    <article class="ba-body">
      <p>Triphala literally means “three fruits”. It combines dried Amalaki (Indian gooseberry), Haritaki and Bibhitaki in equal measure.</p><p>It is one of the most widely used traditional formulations and is usually taken in the evening with warm water.</p>
      <h2 id="highlights">Highlights</h2><ul class="ba-hl"><li>Triphala = Amalaki + Haritaki + Bibhitaki.</li><li>Taste: tangy, slightly bitter and astringent.</li><li>Traditionally taken in warm water before bed.</li></ul>
      <h2 id="s0">The three fruits</h2><p>Amalaki is tart and bright; Haritaki and Bibhitaki are more bitter and astringent. Together they create Triphala's distinctive taste.</p><h2 id="s1">A simple evening ritual</h2><p>Stir a teaspoon into a cup of warm water, let it sit for a minute, and sip slowly. A little honey (once the water has cooled slightly) softens the taste.</p>
